\tag{fdip}
\title{Gauge vacua, time correlations and retained fields}
\date{2026-11-11}

\p{A traced spatial loop can be measured at two different lattice
 times. Its correlation depends on the state propagated between
 those measurements. Which state survives a long periodic time
 direction, and what changes when only selected path transports
 are retained?}

\p{The [gauge transfer operator](fdip-007Z) and its
 [physical Hilbert space](fdip-0083) supply the evolution and the
 gauge constraint. Strict kernel positivity identifies their vacuum.
 The [exact coarse path law](fdip-00MQ) then supplies the reference
 measure for retained vacuum fields.}

